'' RUN: a procedure's address taken BEFORE its definition, then direct calls. '@X' declared
'' X with no parameters and no result, every later call bound to that empty declaration, and
'' the build said 'verify: calls X with N arguments, which declares 0' -- and with an
'' aggregate result clang refused it outright ('[0 x i8]' against '[32 x i8]'). A sub, a
'' function, a string result, an aggregate result, and a call between the address and the
'' definition. Output identical to fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target win64-msvc tests/codegen/src/addr-before-def.bas -o tests/codegen/addrbeforedef.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/win64-msvc
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: verify:
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/addrbeforedef.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/addrbeforedef.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: early, direct 6
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: private, direct 1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: private, pointer 1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: public, direct 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: public, pointer 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: twice 6 8
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: words 5 / words 5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: big 10 13 20 23
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: early, pointer 6
